{"name":"Bishop Red","hex":"#c473a9","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bishop","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An overseer of congregations: either any such overseer, generally speaking, or (in Eastern Orthodoxy, Catholicism, Anglicanism, etc.) an official in the church hierarchy (actively or nominally) governing a diocese, supervising the church's priests, deacons, and property in its territory.","A similar official or chief priest in another religion."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To act as a bishop, to perform the duties of a bishop, especially to confirm another's membership in the church.\n\n To confirm (in its other senses).","To confirm (in its other senses)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bishop"},{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bishop","blocks":[{"text":"In Christianity, a bishop is an ordained member of the clergy who is entrusted with a position of authority and oversight in a religious institution. Bishops are normally responsible for the governance and administration of dioceses, although some function in the various Christian denominations and traditions as auxiliaries, apostolic administrators, and as titular bishops."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bishop","wikidata":"Q29182"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red","wikidata":"Q3142"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Byzantine_-_Saint_Ignatius_of_Antioch_-_Walters_4820867.jpg/500px-Byzantine_-_Saint_Ignatius_of_Antioch_-_Walters_4820867.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Byzantine_-_Saint_Ignatius_of_Antioch_-_Walters_4820867.jpg/1280px-Byzantine_-_Saint_Ignatius_of_Antioch_-_Walters_4820867.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Byzantine_-_Saint_Ignatius_of_Antioch_-_Walters_4820867.jpg/500px-Byzantine_-_Saint_Ignatius_of_Antioch_-_Walters_4820867.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ignatius, bishop of Antioch, student of John the Apostle","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AByzantine_-_Saint_Ignatius_of_Antioch_-_Walters_4820867.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Augustine_Lateran.jpg/250px-Augustine_Lateran.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/44/Augustine_Lateran.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Augus